      "title": "Compute Integration Watcher",
      "description": "Cross-layer wiring auditor — watches for newly-landed mathematical improvements (Lean proofs, propositions, lemmas, axiom→theorem upgrades, witness data) on `origin/main` AND on open PRs, and checks whether each one has been wired into the production compute chain. Complements `local/compute-audit` (which scans for performance/correctness antipatterns inside scripts).  Runs in two modes: REACTIVE (watch new commits / PR events) and IDLE-SWEEP (walk all existing content blocks and audit wiring).",
